  "techniqueSlugs": [],
  "criticalTechniques": [],
  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 4 and takes 10 minutes to prepare and 35 minutes to cook. Red lentils are simmered with onion, carrot and spices until completely soft, then blended smooth and finished with a sizzled butter and smoked paprika drizzle. It is one of the simplest and most satisfying soups in the Turkish repertoire."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tip: add the lemon juice only at the end, just before serving. Acid added too early can toughen the lentils slightly and mutes the fresh citrus brightness."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
