      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the olive oil in the stockpot over a medium heat. Add the onion and carrot and cook, stirring occasionally, for 8 minutes until softened. Add the garlic and cook for 1 more minute."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the cumin, smoked paprika, turmeric and tomato puree. Stir well and cook for 2 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the rinsed lentils and 1.4 litres of water. Bring to the boil, then reduce the heat and simmer uncovered for 25 minutes until the lentils are completely soft and starting to break apart."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove from the heat and blend until smooth using the blender. Return to the pot. Season with salt, black pepper and lemon juice. Add a little boiling water if the soup is thicker than you like."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "In a small pan, melt the butter over a medium heat until it foams. Add a generous pinch of smoked paprika, swirl for 30 seconds, then remove from the heat immediately."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ladle the soup into bowls and drizzle the paprika butter over each one. Serve with crusty bread."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Soup is too thick"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Red lentils absorb a lot of liquid as they sit. Stir in a little boiling water after blending until you reach the consistency you want. The soup will thicken further on reheating."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Soup tastes flat"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Season generously with salt and make sure you add the lemon juice at the very end. A squeeze of fresh lemon sharpens the whole bowl. The paprika butter drizzle also adds a great deal."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Blender splatters hot soup"
            },
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Let the soup cool for 5 minutes before blending. Fill the blender no more than half full, hold the lid down firmly with a folded tea towel, and start on the lowest speed."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Known in Turkey as "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "mercimek"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "mercimek corbasi"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", this is the soup that appears on virtually every Turkish table, from roadside cafes to home kitchens. It is eaten for breakfast, lunch and dinner, and is particularly popular through the cooler months. The butter and paprika drizzle is not decorative; it is an integral part of the flavour. Leftover soup thickens overnight and is excellent thinned back with a splash of water the next day."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
